            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"week-6-validate-the-use-how-an-app-is-built\">Week 6 \u2014 Validate the use; how an app is built</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A number can be correctly sourced (week 4) and correctly defended (week 5) and still be <strong>the wrong number\nfor the question</strong>. This week you ask: <em>fit for what purpose, for whom?</em></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>First half:</strong> whose population does your measure cover, which hospitals are missing and why, and what\nhappens when county data is attached to hospitals. You end with your <strong>data card</strong>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Second half:</strong> how a marimo notebook becomes an app, and a <strong>one-screen sketch</strong> of the app you'll build.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
