            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"5-how-an-app-is-built-and-published\">5. How an app is built and published</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A marimo app is just a notebook with <strong>controls</strong> (<code>mo.ui.\u2026</code>) and <strong>outputs</strong> that depend on them. When a\ncontrol changes, marimo re-runs every cell that uses it \u2014 nothing else. That's the whole idea.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Below is a complete tiny app in <strong>two cells</strong>. The code is shown because reading it is the lesson:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>Cell 1 makes a control. <code>mo.ui.dropdown(...)</code> builds the menu; the last line (<code>state</code>) displays it.</li>\n<li>Cell 2 uses <code>state.value</code> \u2014 whatever the user picked. Because it mentions <code>state</code>, marimo re-runs it on\n  every change. It filters to that state, counts hospitals by type, and draws a bar chart with altair.\n  The title says how many rows are behind the chart \u2014 always show that.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
