            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Publishing.</strong> The same file runs as an app with the code hidden: locally, <code>marimo run your_notebook.py</code>\nopens it in the browser in app view. To share it as a link, follow the publishing steps in this week's\nbrief. Before you share: does every chart say how many rows are behind it, and does the app show where its\ndata came from?</span>\n<div class=\"admonition\">\n<span class=\"admonition-title\">Ask your AI \u2014 start your app</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><em>\"In a marimo notebook, my data layer is a DataFrame called <code>layer</code> with columns ______. Build a\none-screen app: one <code>mo.ui.dropdown</code> for ______ and one chart (altair) that shows ______. Put the number\nof rows behind the chart in the chart title. Do not convert 'Not Available' to zero. Explain each line.\"</em></span>\n</blockquote>\n</div></span>"
